WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:39.580
Marilla pessimistically
expected more trouble

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:43.870
since Anne had again
begun to go to school.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.050
But none developed.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:51.850
Maybe because now she sits with Minnie
Andrews, since she can't be with Diana.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:55.360
And she was determined not to be outdone
in any class by Gilbert Blythe.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:00.570
So she flung herself into
her studies heart and soul.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.910
In the month of December,

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.610
Anne and Gilbert were both
promoted into the fifth class

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.040
where was Diana and other friends.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:24.160
All things great are wound
up with all things little.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.470
It might not seem that the decision
of a certain Canadian Premier to include

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.890
Prince Edward Island in a
political tour could have much

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:40.930
or anything to do with the fortunes of
little Anne Shirley at Green Gables.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.530
But it had.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:47.270
Rachel's husband will drive,

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:53.830
and this might be my only chance
to see a real live Premier.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:57.110
Well now, don't worry and just go.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.110
Then, I'll be back around noon tomorrow.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.770
I'm counting on you, Anne.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.680
Have a nice trip.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:09.550
Thereby Marilla and red-hot
politician Mrs. Rachel Lynde

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:13.850
set off for Charlottetown thirty miles away.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:20.780
Hence, while they were enjoying themselves
hugely at the mass meeting,

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:25.870
Anne and Matthew had the cheerful
kitchen all to themselves.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.260
In order to win against Gilbert
Blythe in tomorrow's test,

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.270
Anne studied with grim determination.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:36.110
And Matthew nodded over a
FARMERS' ADVOCATE on the sofa.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:41.950
Matthew, did you ever study geometry
when you went to school?

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.790
W-Well now, no, I didn't.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.600
I wish you had,

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.120
because then you'd be able
to sympathize with me.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:55.940
It is casting a cloud over my whole life.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.720
I'm such a dunce at it, Matthew.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:05.750
Well now, I dunno.
I guess you're all right at anything.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:10.820
Mr. Phillips told me last week in
Blair's store at Carmody

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:20.770
that you was the smartest scholar in
school and was making rapid progress.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:31.420
There's them as runs down Teddy Phillips
and says he ain't much of a teacher,

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.300
but I guess he's all right.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:40.470
But, Mr. Phillips goes up to
see Prissy nearly every evening.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.170
He says it is to help her with her lessons,

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:49.150
but Miranda Sloane is studying for
Queen's too, and she's not very smart.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:52.110
So I think she needed
help a lot more than Prissy.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:54.800
Well now.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.050
I wonder what is Marilla doing now.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:06.830
Mrs. Lynde says if women were allowed to
vote we would soon see a blessed change.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.270
What way do you vote, Matthew?

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:10.650
Conservative.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:12.850
Then I'm Conservative too.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:13.780
Because Gil...

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:17.970
Some of the boys in school are Grits.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:20.680
I guess Mr. Phillips is a Grit too.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.470
Because Prissy Andrews's father is one.

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:27.830
And Ruby Gillis says that
when a man is courting

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:32.780
he always has to agree with the girl's
mother in religion and her father in politics.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:34.820
Is that true?

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:38.340
Well now, I dunno.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.330
Did you ever go courting, Matthew?

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:46.380
Well now, no, I don't remember.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.190
It must be rather interesting.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:55.150
Ruby Gillis says when she grows up she's
going to have many beaus on the string

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:57.700
and have them all crazy about her.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:03.080
But I'd rather have just one in his right mind.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.960
Well, I must finish up my lessons.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.930
I won't open the book Jane
lent me until I'm through.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.400
But it's a terrible temptation.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:20.010
Even when I turn my back on it
I can see it there just as plain.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:24.460
I will lock the book in the
jam closet in the living room.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:27.690
You must NOT give me back the key
until my lessons are done, Matthew.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.510
Not even if I implore
you on my bended knees.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.570
It's ever so much easier to
resist it if you can't get the key.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:37.180
Anne!

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.630
Diana!?

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.430
Whatever is the matter, Diana?

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.780
Has your mother relented at last?

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.540
Oh, Anne, do come quick,
Minnie May is awful sick!

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.950
She's got croup. Young Mary Joe says.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.350
Croup?

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:04.510
Father and Mother are away to town and
there's nobody to go for the doctor.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:10.510
Minnie May is awful bad and
Young Mary Joe doesn't know what to do!

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:12.840
Anne, I'm so scared!

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:15.060
How is Minnie May doing?

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:16.590
Is it really croup?

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:19.340
I don't know. But she can't breathe.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:29.760
Matthew's gone to harness the sorrel
mare to go to Carmody for the doctor.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.220
I don't believe he'll find
the doctor at Carmody.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:36.310
I know that Dr. Blair went to town and
I guess Dr. Spencer would go too.

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:39.370
If only Mrs. Lynde was around...

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.430
Don't cry, Diana!

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.050
I'm sure Matthew will find a doctor.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:50.020
And I know exactly what to do for croup.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:54.610
You forget that Mrs. Hammond
had twins three times.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:59.170
When you look after three pairs of twins
you naturally get a lot of experience.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:02.840
Look. We have a ipecac bottle.
Come on now.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.240
The snow in the wood way is too deep.

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:16.150
We'll have to go through Lover's Lane.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.350
Will he find a doctor?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.920
He will. Don't worry.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:53.690
Anne, although sincerely
sorry for Minnie May,

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:58.870
was far from being insensible
to the romance of the situation

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:02.680
and to the sweetness of once more
sharing that romance with a kindred spirit.

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:22.300
How is Minnie May?

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:26.640
Oh, Diana! It's serious!
It's very serious!

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:29.160
Minnie May!

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.910
Minnie May, are you suffering?

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:41.090
Minnie, answer me!

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:44.180
No, Diana! She can't answer you now.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:49.410
Minnie May has croup all right.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:54.190
She's pretty bad,
but I've seen them worse.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.240
Minnie...

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.010
First we must have lots of hot water.

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:02.150
It doesn't have any water?

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:05.610
Mary Joe, you may
put some wood in the stove.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.780
I'm sorry, but you might
have thought of this before.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:16.960
Please fill two kettles full
of water before lighting the fire.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:21.110
Now, I'll undress Minnie May
to let her breath easily.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:25.350
Diana? Could you try to
find some soft flannel cloths?

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.110
Yes!

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:50.540
Here. Drink this Minnie May.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:56.130
Come on, it's delicious. Open you mouth.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:59.040
Minnie May, please. Drink it.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.070
Oh, Minnie May...

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:43.770
Oh, where is the doctor?

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:47.750
He couldn't find one in Carmody?
He couldn't find one?

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:49.720
Calm down, Diana!

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:55.280
Mary Joe, open that window.
It's too hot in here.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:25.570
Just as Diana had worried,

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:30.340
all the doctors of Carmody had
gone to Charlottetown.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:35.090
So Matthew had to go all
the way to Spencervale.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:38.840
Anne, Minnie May is coughing hard.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.450
Anne, Is she alright?
Is she going to be alright?

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:58.150
Yes, I think so.

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:10.510
It was three o'clock when Matthew came
with a doctor from Spencervale.

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:44.330
Doctor...

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:49.080
Don't worry. The pressing need
for assistance has past.

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:50.880
Minnie May...

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.410
Thank goodness, Minnie May!

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:55.410
Thank goodness!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.620
You gave her the right medicine.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:11.650
I was awfully near giving up in despair.

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:16.280
I gave her every drop of ipecac in that
bottle and when the last dose went down,

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.410
I said to myself...

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:23.860
This is the last
lingering hope and I fear, tis a vain one.

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:30.040
But in about three minutes
she coughed up the phlegm

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:32.430
and began to get better right away.

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:37.050
You must just imagine my relief, doctor,
because I can't express it in words.

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:40.770
Yes, I know. You worked hard!

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:44.360
I'll handle the rest, you go rest.

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:46.790
Yes. Thank you, doctor!

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.290
Anne! Anne!

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:49.910
Thank you, Anne!

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:23.300
Oh, Matthew, isn't it a wonderful morning?

00:16:23.990 --> 00:16:28.700
The world looks like something God
had just imagined for His own pleasure.

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:36.510
I'm so glad Mrs. Hammond
had three pairs of twins after all.

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:42.160
If she hadn't I mightn't
have known what to do for Minnie May.

00:16:43.550 --> 00:16:46.790
But, oh, I'm so sleepy.

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:49.300
I can't go to school.

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:52.220
I just know I couldn't keep my eyes open.

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:56.470
But I hate to stay home, for Gil...

00:16:56.720 --> 00:17:00.500
No. Some of the others will
get head of the class.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:09.850
Well now, don't worry.
I guess you'll manage all right.

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:12.630
You just go right to bed
and have a good sleep.

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:30.560
That little redheaded girl Anne is
as smart as they make 'em.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.950
I tell you she saved that baby's life,

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:40.240
for it would have been too late
by the time I got there.

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:46.190
She seems to have a skill and presence of
mind wonderful in a child of her age.

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:50.750
I never saw anything like the eyes of her
when she was explaining the case to me.

00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:53.540
I'll be off then.

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:57.040
Thank you, Doctor.

00:17:57.400 --> 00:18:00.490
No. You should thank that little girl.

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.020
Welcome home!

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.020
Did you see the Premier?

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:28.700
What did he look like Marilla?

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:33.050
Well, he never got to be Premier
on account of his looks.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:35.750
Well, I am going to get you some food.

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:37.360
I guess you're hungry.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:39.420
I truly am hungry.

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:42.540
Matthew has been telling me about last night.

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:45.590
I must say it was
fortunate you knew what to do.

00:18:45.590 --> 00:18:47.710
I wouldn't have had any idea myself,

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:50.980
for I never saw a case of croup.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.810
Mrs. Barry was here this afternoon.

00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:03.250
She wanted to see you, but I
wouldn't wake you up.

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:08.240
She says you saved Minnie May's life,

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:11.410
and she is very sorry she acted as she did.

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:16.650
She says she knows now
you didn't mean to set Diana drunk,

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:22.650
and she hopes you'll forgive
her and be good friends with Diana again.

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:27.700
You're to go
over this evening if you like.

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:29.900
Oh, Marilla, can I go right now,

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:31.880
without washing my dishes?

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:33.840
I'll wash them when I come back,

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:38.290
but I cannot tie myself down
to anything so unromantic

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:41.040
as dishwashing at this thrilling moment!

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:44.950
Yes, don't worry about the dishes,
but you have to eat something.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:46.160
Hey, Anne!

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:47.160
Anne!

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:53.280
I might as well call to the wind.

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:56.780
She's gone without a cap or wrap, It'll be a
mercy if she doesn't catch her death of cold.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:09.700
Diana!

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:11.060
Anne!

00:20:56.700 --> 00:21:01.980
If you love me as I love you,

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:07.290
nothing but death can part us two.

00:21:20.850 --> 00:21:22.020
Diana.

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:31.070
I'm going to ask Mr. Phillips to let us sit
together in school again.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:34.250
I was thinking in doing the same.

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.790
It's the first time I'm making a taffy.
Will it be all right?

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:47.580
Don't worry. We'll just have to pull now.

00:21:48.150 --> 00:21:49.300
Come, pull!

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:03.690
This is fun!

00:22:03.690 --> 00:22:04.740
Isn't it?

00:22:09.070 --> 00:22:11.020
How is everything?

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:18.020
Hey!

00:22:26.850 --> 00:22:28.860
Well, well.

00:22:52.630 --> 00:22:53.940
Thank you, Mrs. Barry!

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:04.390
Goodbye! See you again tomorrow!

00:23:04.690 --> 00:23:06.820
Good night, Anne!

00:23:08.230 --> 00:23:10.160
Good night!

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:19.680
We had an elegant tea.

00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:25.050
Mrs. Barry had the very best china set out,
just as if I was real company.

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:28.910
I can't tell you what a thrill it gave me.

00:23:29.060 --> 00:23:31.760
It made me feel that I've grown up!

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:36.660
I'm perfectly happy, yes,
in spite of my red hair.

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:39.510
Just at present I
have a soul above red hair.

00:23:40.040 --> 00:23:43.880
You see before you a
perfectly happy person, Marilla.

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:47.710
I know you went through much today,

00:23:47.710 --> 00:23:50.160
but you have school tomorrow, rest early.

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:52.530
Yes.
Good night, Marilla.

00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:22.840
Diana invites Anne
to the Debate Club Concert.

00:24:23.140 --> 00:24:26.120
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:27.930
Diana's Birthday

00:24:28.020 --> 00:24:29.210
Please watch!
